Animations aren’t just for fancy websites or landing pages. Even subtle, simple animations can make your site feel smoother, more polished, and more enjoyable to use. In this post, I’ll show you how I used basic animations with Framer Motion and React to create a smooth experience on a component I call Smooth Reveal. I made a small demo to show this in action. Check it out here Here’s what happens in the demo: Navbar fades in from the top. Main section smoothly reveals the text WI and LD, with a video expanding in the center. Footer slides in with content and a CTA button. 🧩 Full Code Overview Navbar.tsx A simple navbar with animated hover effect and theme switcher:
